<h3>Methodology Note</h3>
<p>All statistics in this report are derived directly from the UNODC-based dataset ({R['overview']['total_rows']:,} observations across {R['overview']['unique_countries']} countries, {R['overview']['year_range'][0]}–{R['overview']['year_range'][1]}). The median is used as the primary central-tendency measure due to the highly right-skewed distribution of homicide rates. No values have been imputed or estimated. Regional classifications are based on standard UN geographic groupings. Decade-over-decade changes are computed using unweighted means of country-year observations within each decade.</p>

